  "title": "Calls through overridden methods",
  "summary": "Find references on an override includes the calls made through the methods it overrides, which may dispatch to it",
  "prose": "`shape.area()` on a `Shape&` may run `Circle::area`, so it is among the\nreferences of the override. A call through `Circle` never runs\n`Shape::area`, so it is not among the references of the method overridden.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [
    "clangd#1558"
  ],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "struct Shape {\n    virtual double area() const = 0;\n};\n\nstruct Circle : Shape {\n    double area() const override {\n        return 3.0;\n    }\n};\n\ndouble through_base(const Shape& shape) {\n    return shape.area();\n}\n\ndouble through_circle(const Circle& circle) {\n    return circle.area();\n}\n",
